SCOPE — read this before relying on the licence.

This licence covers the source code of EDEXO-Compare. It does NOT cover:

  * the data - the data/ folder and the data tables generated into the code -
    which is licensed under Creative Commons BY-NC-SA 3.0 (non-commercial,
    share-alike); see data/LICENSE-DATA.txt, which also says what counts as
    data and why;
  * src/shared/gggCatalogue.ts, the edGGG catalogue of green gas giants
    (https://ed-ggg.github.io/edggg/, CMDR Arcanic), included with credit and
    under its author's terms;
  * the species photographs under data/species/<genus>/<genus>_photos/, of
    either kind, described below: they are screenshots of Elite Dangerous, and
    the game and its artwork are Frontier Developments' and under Frontier's
    terms;
  * Elite Dangerous game content, artwork and species names, which are the
    property of Frontier Developments plc;
  * data/exomastery/region-map.json, which is MIT-licensed by Ben Peddell and
    carries its own notice in data/exomastery/region-map.LICENSE.txt.

THE PHOTOGRAPHS — there are two kinds, and the app says which is which.

Every photograph displayed in the app carries a credit beneath it. There is no
unlabelled image, and the credit is the statement of origin:

  * "Photo by Bahuckel - CMDR <name>" means the photograph was contributed.
    That commander took it themselves, in their own game, and gave it to this
    project knowingly - either the project owner's own work, or a commander who
    photographed a species for this project or offered an existing capture in
    support of it. These files are named individually in
    data/species/photo-credits.json.

  * "Photo from: https://ed-dsn.net/ and its respective owner" means the
    photograph is sourced from the ED-DSN community. It is here with ED-DSN's
    agreement while replacements are photographed, and it is not this project's
    to sublicense. This is the standing credit, applied to any image not named
    in that manifest, so an image cannot pass as contributed by omission.

Neither kind is covered by this licence. Two rights sit in every one of them
and neither belongs to this project: the game artwork, which is Frontier's, and
the capture itself, which belongs to the commander who took it. A contributor
gave this project permission to use their photograph here; they did not
transfer ownership of it, and this licence cannot pass on what it was never
given.

See NOTICE.md for the full attribution and for how to request removal of an
image. Any rights holder who would prefer theirs removed can ask, and it will
be, with no justification needed.

